Acceptance (Flight-2) Unit_Thermal Cycle:

At all Performance temperatures during Acceptance Thermal Cycle, these parameters will be measured:
•	RF output with -10 dBm input (OQPSK waveform) in High Gain state (each band)
•	Maximum gain in Low Gain state (each band)
•	Spectral Emissions (each band)
o	OQPSK spectral mask, for max gain and min gain
o	Spurious emissions and harmonics
•	Gain and phase characterization data for each attenuator setting (each band)
o	Gain variation
o	Differential gain (H / V)
o	Differential phase (H/V)
•	Input/output VSWR (each band)
•	Command & response, operating modes, RF output stabilization
•	Power consumption (each band)
•	Voltage and temperature telemetry with timestamps  

At all Functional temperatures during Acceptance Thermal Cycle, these parameters will be measured:
•	RF output power with -10 dBm input (CW tone) in High Gain state (each band)
o	DC power consumption
•	Control and telemetry 
•	Run ATE software to log voltage and temperature telemetry during tests.
